# Copy to .env here or one folder up (outside the repo) and fill in; on a VPS use deploy/.env.template instead.
# Defaults: server/formwright/config.py
# (Formwright Parts: server/formwright/shop/quote.py, ShopSettings). META_KEY and FW_META_API_KEY are accepted too.
META_API_KEY=

# Model routing. The Contributor tier is cheap for dev/test runs (content may be used to train Meta models).
# FW_MODEL_DESIGNER=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
# FW_MODEL_FAST=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
# FW_MODEL_FREE=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
# FW_MODEL_CRITIC=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
# Let anonymous visitors (judges) pick Muse Wonder as the designer
# FW_DEMO_WONDER=1

# Budgets in USD. FW_DAILY_BUDGET_USD caps everyone together: past 80% of it the strongest designer is
# skipped, at 100% only replays, sliders and downloads work. For a public demo divide the credit left by the
# days it stays up, e.g. $150 over 5-16 Nov: about 10.
# FW_JOB_BUDGET_USD=0.60
# FW_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=25
# The share of it anonymous visitors may spend together, however many addresses they come from; the rest stays
# for people with a sign-in link (judges, farm operators, the Telegram bot)
# FW_ANON_BUDGET_SHARE=0.75

# Wall-clock limits in seconds: past the deadline a design job wraps up with its latest version, a minute
# later it is stopped. A question to the person waits FW_ASK_TIMEOUT_S, and the wait does not count.
# FW_DESIGN_DEADLINE_S=600
# FW_SIDE_DEADLINE_S=180
# FW_ASK_TIMEOUT_S=180

# Blur human faces (SAM 3.1) in uploaded photos before any other model sees them
# FW_BLUR_FACES=1

# Slicing (found automatically in the default install location). Formwright Parts needs it for binding quotes:
# without it customers see only the instant range and an operator quotes by hand. The quotes were calibrated on
# OrcaSlicer 2.4.2 (2.3.0 cannot slice the A1 preset from the command line).
# FW_ORCA_BIN=C:\Program Files\OrcaSlicer\orca-slicer.exe
# FW_ORCA_PROFILES=C:\Program Files\OrcaSlicer\resources\profiles

# Formwright Parts. Prices are in tenge; the US dollar figure next to each uses this fixed rate (KZT per USD)
# FW_USD_KZT=520
# The farm's OrcaSlicer machine preset: quotes use it until a farm printer is registered (scripts/shop_seed.py adds
# one), and it is the studio's default printer and the printer the agent's checks assume
# FW_FARM_PRESET=bambu-lab-a1-0-4-nozzle

# Geometry worker processes for checks, renders and export (up to 1 GB of heap each): 1 on a 4 GB server
# FW_GEOM_WORKERS=2

# PCB pipeline. packages/pcb is its own npm package; dev.ps1 builds its sandboxed worker when it is missing, or by hand:
#   cd packages/pcb && npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm run bundle
# The server runs only <FW_PCB_DIR>/dist. One worker, restarted after every build; a build that takes longer than
# FW_PCB_TIMEOUT seconds is killed.
# FW_PCB_DIR=<repo>/packages/pcb
# FW_PCB_POOL_SIZE=1
# FW_PCB_TIMEOUT=90

# Open weights (OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions endpoint). Muse Spark Open on Baseten:
# FW_OPEN_BASE_URL=https://inference.baseten.co/v1
# FW_OPEN_API_KEY=
# FW_OPEN_MODEL=meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026
# FW_MODEL_CRITIC=meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026
# Roles the open model takes: the independent critic, classification (the request's pack and photos, and the
# second opinion on spare-part requests), English for prompts. Add snap_name to name Snap finds there too (slower).
# It never decides a refusal: Muse Spark does. The JSON schema goes into its prompt and its reasoning effort is low;
# an answer without the schema's keys is logged and Muse Spark takes that call over.
# FW_OPEN_ROLES=critic,classify,english
# FW_OPEN_TIMEOUT_S=60
# Its price per million tokens, so budgets count it. The default 0 is right for a self-hosted GPU; on Baseten use
# its list price for Muse Spark Open (30 Oct 2026), shown here. Cached input is counted at the input price.
# FW_OPEN_PRICE_IN_PER_M=1.25
# FW_OPEN_PRICE_OUT_PER_M=4.25
# Self-hosted alternative: Muse Glimmer on Modal, see infra/modal_glimmer.py

# Behind reverse proxies: how many proxies of ours append to X-Forwarded-For. The visitor's address (for the
# per-address cap on anonymous use) is the entry this many places from the right, so whatever a visitor writes
# further left never counts. The container sets 1: one TLS proxy (Caddy, nginx) in front, the port published on
# 127.0.0.1. A CDN in front of that proxy: 2. Nothing in front: 0, with FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS="" for uvicorn.
# Never FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS="*". Unset (-1): 1 when uvicorn trusts every sender, else the address uvicorn reports.
# FW_PROXY_HOPS=1

# Storage: the SQLite database and files (the container uses /app/data). server/scripts/ship_runs.py moves recorded
# runs from one data dir to another (e.g. to the live server's volume)
# FW_DATA_DIR=<repo>/data

# Integrations
# Public address of this instance: phone-handoff QR codes, login links and share previews use it
# (deploy/compose.yaml sets https://FW_DOMAIN)
# FW_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:5400
# vite's port when it serves the web app next to the API, so pages opened on the API's port go there (dev.ps1 sets it)
# FW_WEB_DEV_PORT=5400
# Telegram bot: photos, voice notes, the Order print button and /part, which order through Formwright Parts.
# It long-polls, so one token runs in one place: leave it blank on every other machine
# FW_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
# Axo's external order API (the founder's existing business): only POST /api/projects/{id}/order sends to it; the web
# and the Telegram bot order through Formwright Parts instead
# FW_AXO_API_URL=
# FW_AXO_API_KEY=
